# Snyk (https://snyk.io) policy file, patches or ignores known vulnerabilities.
version: v1.5.0
ignore:
  SNYK-JS-CODEMIRROR-10494092:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          ReDoS in codemirror@5.65.21, pulled in transitively by our direct
          dependency easymde@2.21.0. easymde's only consumer is
          NoteEditor.svelte, a private per-user job-tracking notes field —
          content is always self-authored by the same user who reads it back,
          never rendered from another user's or otherwise untrusted input, so
          the exploitable path does not exist here.
          No safe fix is available: easymde 2.21.0 is the latest stable
          release and still pins codemirror ^5.65.15; the only CodeMirror-6
          line is a pre-release (3.0.0-alpha/beta) with a fully incompatible
          API, and forcing a codemirror override under 2.21.0 breaks it at
          runtime (CM5-only calls). Revisit when easymde ships a stable CM6
          release, or budget a NoteEditor migration off easymde before this
          expires.
        expires: 2026-11-13T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-08-13T00:00:00.000Z
  SNYK-JS-DEEPMERGE-19964053:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          Prototype Pollution in deepmerge@4.3.1, pulled in transitively by
          @sveltejs/vite-plugin-svelte, which @sveltejs/kit declares as a PEER
          dependency and not a dependency — it is a Vite plugin, so it runs at
          BUILD time only and is in neither the SSR server bundle nor anything
          the browser loads. Its one call site is mergeConfigs() in
          utils/options.js, which merges the plugin's own option objects: our
          svelte.config.js and our vite config, both statically authored in
          this repository. Polluting a prototype needs attacker-controlled keys
          in the merged object, and nothing a request carries ever reaches it,
          so the exploitable path does not exist here.
          No fix is available: deepmerge 4.3.1 IS the latest published release
          (there is no 4.3.2 and no 5.x), and @sveltejs/vite-plugin-svelte
          7.3.0 — also the latest — still declares deepmerge ^4.3.1, so neither
          upgrading nor a pnpm override reaches a patched version. Revisit when
          deepmerge publishes a fixed release, or when vite-plugin-svelte drops
          the dependency; either ends this ignore without a code change here.
        expires: 2026-12-20T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-09-20T00:00:00.000Z
